.Dd @MDOCDATE@
.Dt CLOWN-RESTART 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm clown-restart
.Nd queue a restart of a live clown session
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm clown restart
.Fl -session Ar key
.Op Fl -when Cm idle
.Op Fl -reason Ar text
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm clown restart
is the clown half of a spinclass session restart (spinclass#419, spinclass FDR
0037).
spinclass authorizes and records the restart, then runs the operator's
.Sy [session-entry].restart
hand-off, normally
.Dl clown restart --session {principal} --when {when} --reason {reason}
which reaches the live
.Nm clown
frontend of
.Ar key
over its control socket,
.Pa $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/clown/control/ Ns Ar key Ns Pa .sock ,
and queues the request.
It returns as soon as the frontend has queued it.
The command authorizes nothing: a queued request only makes the frontend ask
spinclass again at the next idle transition.
.Pp
Only
.Fl -when Cm idle ,
the default, is accepted.
A newer request replaces a queued one.
.Ss The idle transition
The frontend's idle trigger is the self-close Stop hook (clown#287): after
each turn the agent's
.Cm clown idle-notify
pokes the frontend, which runs, in this fixed order:
.Bl -enum
.It
.Ic spinclass close-self-run ,
as on every idle transition.
.It
Only when a restart is queued: it takes the request and runs
.Ic spinclass restart-preflight
with
.Ev CLOWN_SESSION_ID
set to the session's principal.
The preflight prints one JSON line,
.Li {\(dqverdict\(dq:\(dqrestart\(dq|\(dqnone\(dq|\(dqrefused\(dq,\(dqreason\(dq:...,\(dqwhen\(dq:...} ,
and consumes the request itself, so a relaunched session does not restart
again.
Only
.Li restart
proceeds.
.Li none
(for example because the close in step 1 landed),
.Li refused ,
a non-zero exit, a timeout, or anything but exactly one such line drops the
request and leaves the session running.
.El
.Pp
Each decision is appended to
.Pa $XDG_STATE_HOME/clown/close-self-run.log .
.Ss The restart
On a
.Li restart
verdict the frontend first runs, while the provider still runs, the profile
check the relaunch will run (the
.Cm clown resume
check of FDR 0022: the launch's
.Fl -profile
against the session's recorded pin, with no launcher approval).
If it would refuse (the profile changed, no longer resolves, or cannot be
pinned) the restart is dropped, the reason is logged, and the session keeps
running.
.Pp
An attached session then gets a 30 second countdown.
Inside a
.Xr posh 1
session
.Pq Ev POSH_SESSION No set
whose
.Ic posh modal --probe
answers, the countdown is posh's app modal: exit 0 proceeds and exit 10 (a
viewer cancelled) keeps the session running; exit 11 or 12 (posh showed
nothing) falls back to the inline countdown, and any other end of a modal
that was shown proceeds without a second wait.
Any other attached terminal gets a one-line
.Dq restart pending
notice on standard error and the same wait, with no cancel.
A detached session restarts at once.
A turn that starts during the countdown (the self-close plugin's
UserPromptSubmit hook,
.Cm clown idle-notify --busy )
cancels the restart; spinclass has already consumed the request, so the
requester asks again.
.Pp
The frontend then stops the provider as an external
.Dv SIGTERM
would (claude, its plugin servers including the serve bridge, and an
.Fl -agent-scope
unit), waits up to 15 seconds for every socket under
.Pa $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/clown/serve/ Ns Ar principal Ns Pa /
to stop answering (a relaunched bridge refuses a live one), and replaces
itself with the
.Nm clown
found on
.Ev PATH ,
so a new build is picked up.
It is the same process, terminal and multiplexer pane.
The relaunch has the launch's own resolved flags, including
.Fl -profile ,
with claude's
.Fl -session-id
or
.Fl -resume
replaced by
.Fl -resume Ar principal ,
and
.Ev CLOWN_SESSION_ID Ns = Ns Ar principal ;
the profile check of
.Cm clown resume
applies unchanged; a profile edited between the dry run and the relaunch is
still refused there, after the stop.
The resumed session's system prompt starts with
.Dq restarted: Ar reason ,
the reason spinclass's verdict gave (one line of printable text, at most 300
characters; a fixed text when it gave none), never the one passed to
.Nm clown restart .
.Pp
A provider that has not exited 30 seconds after the stop keeps the session:
the restart is abandoned and a later exit does not relaunch.
If the serve socket stays live, no
.Nm clown
is on
.Ev PATH ,
or the exec fails, the frontend says so on standard error, names
.Cm clown resume Ar principal ,
and exits without relaunching.
.Pp
A restart is not a close: nothing on the restart path revokes or releases the
session's identity.
The frontend never runs
.Ic troupe mint-revoke ;
the relaunch re-runs the idempotent
.Ic troupe mint
for the same principal and registers the same presence key.
.Ss Which frontends answer
Every launch that runs its provider as a child binds the control socket (not
.Fl -naked ,
not the exec-replacing
.Cm codex ,
not
.Fl -print-launch-plan ) .
Only a claude launch with the idle trigger armed queues; the others refuse
with a message saying why.
A second frontend for the same key does not take over a live control socket,
and a frontend that exits removes the socket only while it is still its own.
The socket is not reachable from an
.Fl -agent-scope
unit: the unit's
.Pa /run/user
is a tmpfs holding only the sockets bound into it.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Root of the control and serve sockets.
.It Ev CLOWN_RESTARTED_REASON
Set by a restarting frontend for the relaunched one, which reads and unsets it
before starting anything.
Not for manual use.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Nm clown restart
exits
.Sy 0
once the request is queued,
.Sy 1
when it is not, with the reason on standard error:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Li no live clown frontend for Ar key
No frontend listens on the control socket.
.It Li restart needs an idle trigger; Ar provider Li has none
The frontend runs a provider without the idle trigger
(claude with the trigger off names the gate instead).
.El
.Pp
A usage error exits
.Sy 2 .
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr clown 1 ,
.Xr clown-presence 1 ,
.Xr posh 1
.Sh STANDARDS
spinclass FDR 0037 (session restart), FDR 0020 (agent-scope confinement).
